{title: 2,300 Evenings and Mornings}
{subtitle: Daniel 8:1–27}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×9
| [Bmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
One [C#]horn was higher than the [G#m]rest
It charged [B]west, [C#]north, and [D#m]south
No [Bmaj7]animal [C#]could stand against [D#m]its power
It [Bmaj7]did as it [C#]pleased and grew [D#m]great
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Then a [Bmaj7]male goat came from the [C#]west
Crossing [D#m]the earth without touching ground
A [Bmaj7]conspicuous horn between its [C#]eyes
It rushed at the [G#m]ram in furious [A#]power
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [D#m]large horn is [C#]broken [A#m]off
[B]Four horns grow toward [C#]the four winds of [D#m]heaven
Out of one [C#]comes [A#m]a small [B]horn
[G#m]Growing exceedingly [A#]great toward the [D#m]south
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
It reaches the host of heaven
Throwing stars [B]down to the [C#]earth to be tram[D#m]pled
It sets itself [C#]up against the [G#m]Prince
Taking a[B]way the [C#]daily sacri[D#m]fice
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[B]Truth is flung to the [C#]ground
Whatever it [D#m]does, it prospered
I [B]heard a holy one spea[C#]king
Asking [G#m]how long this desolation [A#sus4]will [A#]last
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [D#m]large horn is [C#]broken [A#m]off
[B]Four horns grow [C#]toward the four winds [D#m]of heaven
Out of [C#]one [A#m]comes a [B]small [G#m]horn
Growing exceeding[A#sus4]ly great toward the [D#m]south
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[B]Gabriel ex[C#]plains the vision to [D#m]me
[B]The ram repre[C#]sents Media and [D#m]Persia
The [B]goat is the [C#]king of [D#m]Greece
The [B]large horn is [C#]the first [D#m]king
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
Four [B]kingdoms will arise from his na[C#]tion
But they [D#m]will not have his power
A [B]fierce-look-ing king will a[C#]rise
A [G#m]master of intrigue and [A#sus4]cunning
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The [D#m]large horn is [C#]broken [A#m]off
[B]Four horns grow toward [C#]the four winds of [D#m]heaven
Out of one [C#]comes [A#m]a small [B]horn
[G#m]Growing exceedingly [A#sus4]great toward the [D#m]south
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
He will de[B]stroy the mighty and the holy [D#m]people
Through his [B]cunning, de[C#]ceit will pros[D#m]per
He will ex[B]alt himself in his [D#m]heart
But he will be bro[B]ken, [C#]not by human [D#m]hand
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[B]It will take 2,300 evenings [C#]and morn[D#m]ings
Then [B]the sanctuary will be re[C#]stored to its [D#m]rightful state
{end_of_verse}
